hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15614","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hisham, meaning al-Dastuway, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abi Rashid al-Hubrani, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Recite the Quran, and do not go to excess in it, and do not turn away from it, and do not eat by it, and do not seek increase by it."
"15615","And he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the traders are the wicked. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah made trade lawful. He said: Yes, but they speak and lie, and swear and sin."
"15616","He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed the defiantly disobedient are the people of the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the defiantly disobedient. He said: Women. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers and our sisters and our wives. He said: Yes, but when they are given they are not grateful, and when they are tested they are not patient."
"15617","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid, he said: My father narrated to me, from Tamim ibn Mahmud, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding three: the pecking of the crow, and the spreading of the beast of prey, and that a man fix his place as the camel fixes its place."
"15618","Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, al-Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me that Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam narrated to him, from Tamim ibn Mahmud al-Laythi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl al-Ansari, that he said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade in prayer three things: the pecking of the crow, and the spreading of the beast of prey, and that a man fix one place as the camel fixes its place."
"15619","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Jafar ibn al-Hakam, from Tamim ibn Mahmud, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us three things, then he mentioned it."
"15620","Waki narrated to us, from al-Dastuway, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi Rashid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Recite the Quran, and do not eat by it, and do not seek increase by it, and do not turn away from it, and do not go to excess in it."
"15751","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather, he said: Mu'awiyah wrote to Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl: Teach the people what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He gathered them and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Learn the Quran, and when you learn it, do not exaggerate in it, nor turn away from it, nor eat by it, nor seek much by it."
"15752","Then he said: The traders are the wicked. They said: O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah permitted sale and forbidden usury? He said: Yes, but they swear and sin."
"15753","Then he said: The dissolute are the people of the Fire. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and who are the dissolute? He said: Women. They said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers and our daughters and our sisters? He said: Yes, but when they are given they are not grateful, and when they are tried they are not patient."
"15754","Then he said: The rider greets the walker, and the walker greets the sitter, and the fewer greet the more. Whoever answers the greeting, it is for him, and whoever does not answer, there is nothing for him."
"15755","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, my father narrated to me, from Tamim ibn Mahmud, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade three things: the pecking of the crow, and the spreading of the beast, and that a man fix his standing place. Uthman said: In the mosque, as the camel fixes its place."
"15756","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Quran, and do not exaggerate in it, nor turn away from it, nor eat by it, nor seek much by it."
"15757","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The traders are the wicked. A man said: O Prophet of Allah, has not Allah permitted sale? He said: They speak and lie, and swear and sin."
"15758","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl al-Ansari, that Mu'awiyah said to him: When you come to my camp, stand and inform of what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite the Quran, and do not exaggerate in it, nor turn away from it, nor eat by it, nor seek much by it."
"15759","Affan narrated to us, Musa ibn Khalaf Abu Khalaf narrated to us, and he was counted among the Abdal, and he mentioned another hadith similar to it."
